cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use twelveswaras in your research, please cite the version you used, as below."
title: "twelveswaras: an open-source raaga recognizer for Carnatic and Hindustani music"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sankaran
    given-names: Sathya
repository-code: "https://github.com/twelveswaras/twelveswaras"
url: "https://twelveswaras.com"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
# The concept DOI: resolves to the latest release on Zenodo. Version DOIs are listed there.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24096813
date-released: "2026-11-10"
abstract: >-
  twelveswaras is an open-source "Shazam for raagas": given a recording of Indian classical
  music (Carnatic or Hindustani) it identifies the raaga among 70 (40 Carnatic, 30 Hindustani),
  shows the top three candidates with calibrated confidence and the detected tonic (Sa), and
  helps the listener learn to hear that raaga. The tonic is estimated from the drone; a
  tonic-normalized, windowed Time-Delayed Melody Surface (TDMS) feeds an XGBoost classifier,
  whose evidence is fused with per-raaga second-order Markov chains over the sung swaras, which
  capture the order of notes that the surface cannot see. The project reports its measurements
  openly, including on a real-world benchmark of phone, concert and broadcast audio, a tonic
  benchmark against hand-annotated tonics, and negative results. It is paired with a
  community-contributed, openly-licensed data commons (CC-BY-4.0), and is a non-commercial
  public good stewarded in the neutral twelveswaras organization, not owned by any company.
keywords:
  - Carnatic music
  - Hindustani music
  - Indian art music
  - raaga recognition
  - tonic estimation
  - music information retrieval
  - TDMS
  - Markov chains
  - XGBoost
